Jesus commanded his followers: “Go therefore and make disciples of people of all the nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the holy spirit, teaching them to observe all the things I have commanded you. ” Thus, we must teach the things that Christ commanded.
To observe a command means to “conform one’s action ” to a command — to obey, or keep, it. How, then, do we teach someone to observe, or obey, the things that Christ commanded?
