Let us find answers to these questions by considering the life and career of Timothy.
Timothy’s Background
Timothy grew up in Lystra, a small town in the Roman province of Galatia. He likely came in touch with Christianity as a teenager when Paul preached in Lystra about 47 C.E.
Timothy quickly gained an excellent reputation among the local Christian brothers. On returning to Lystra two years later and learning of his progress, Paul chose Timothy to serve as his missionary companion.
What training did Timothy receive, and how did he respond? Timothy was reared in a religiously divided home.
His father was a Greek, and his mother, Eunice, and his grandmother Lois were of Jewish origin.
How did Timothy benefit from upbuilding Christian companionship?
He cultivated a close friendship with Paul, a dynamic person.
Paul wrote: “You have closely followed my teaching, my course of life, my purpose, my faith, my long - suffering, my love, my endurance. ”
Like Timothy, you need to make a careful examination of “the holy writings. ” Studying may not be your favorite activity, but remember that Timothy had to ‘ train himself with godly devotion as his aim. ’
